      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Salonika‑Palestine Investment Company, founded in 1921, bought land in Tel Aviv to spark commercial ties with Jewish settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florentin%2C_Tel_Aviv",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1924, the company sent an envoy to purchase land south of Herzl Street, near the Jaffa‑Jerusalem railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florentin%2C_Tel_Aviv",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1990s saw abandoned garages and buildings converted into artist workshops, sparking Florentin’s bohemian renaissance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
